-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",261,{
[8321]="700033CA\n1\tDefeat hill-toads (total: 8)\tLobelia the toad is hiding among the hill-toads in the Frogmoors, the marsh just north of Frogmorton. Milo Hornblower has asked you to clear out enough toads in the Frogmoors for Lobelia the Toad to show herself.\n2\tWith enough toads cleared out, Lobelia the Toad should emerge somewhere in the Frogmoors, north of The Floating Log. Milo Hornblower has asked you to subdue the wild toad he has named Lobelia.\t\n3\tTalk to Milo Hornblower\tMilo Hornblower is waiting by The Floating Log in Frogmorton. You should let Milo know of your success in capturing Lobelia the Toad.\n",
[8322]="7004E1DC\n1\tTalk to Queen Regent Erna and aid the people of Dale\tErna can be found within the Great-keep in Dale. King Thorin III has asked you to speak to the other leaders of the North and aid them in hastening their preparations for the coming of Vethúg Wintermind.\n2\tDale-folk can be found throughout Dale. Erna has not ordered her people to Erebor, but she will allow them to depart for safety if they wish it. You should urge the people of Dale to seek shelter in Erebor.\t\n3\tTalk to Master Dagrun and aid the people of Lake-town\tDagrun can be found within the Master's Manor in Lake-town. After aiding the people of Dale, you should continue on to Lake-town and aid the Lake-men as best you can.\n4\tCollect the Master's curfew notices\tThe pile of curfew notices can be found behind Dagrun in the Master's Manor in Lake-town. Dagrun has asked you to post curfew notices throughout Lake-town, and has offered a number of water-skins to the dwarves of Erebor. You should pick up the notices before leaving the Master's Manor.\n5\tPost the Master's curfew notices in Lake-town (total: 10)\030Collect water-skins in Lake-town (total: 8)\tNotices can be posted throughout Lake-town. Water-skins can be found around Lake-town. Dagrun has asked you to post curfew notices, and in return, she has offered a number of water-skins to aid the dwarves of Erebor.\n6\tTalk to King Thranduil and aid the Elves of Felegoth\tKing Thranduil can be found in Felegoth. You have aided the people of Lake-town in preparing, and you should now travel to Felegoth and aid King Thranduil and the Elves of Eryn Lasgalen in preparing for the coming of Vethúg Wintermind.\n7\tCollect quivers of arrows in Felegoth (total: 6)\030Collect crates of provisions in Felegoth (total: 6)\030Collect handfuls of straw in Felegoth (total: 6)\tQuivers of arrows can be found near the dungeons of Felegoth, crates of provisions can be found in the wine cellar, and straw can be found near the trapdoors of Felegoth. King Thranduil has asked you to help ease the burden of travel to Erebor by packing several barrels with supplies to be shipped to Loeglond for the coming battle at Erebor.\n8\tPack barrels of supplies to send through the water-gate (total: 6)\tBarrels can be found nearby the trapdoors of Felegoth. You have gathered many supplies and straw and should now use what you have gathered to pack barrels for the Elves of Felegoth.\n9\tTalk to King Thorin III\tKing Thorin III can be found before his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain. You have aided all the peoples of the North and should now return to King Thorin III at Erebor.\n",
[8323]="70032D8A\n1\tSearch the corpses of Orcs for a cause of death (total: 8)\tOrc-corpses can be found throughout Baiúrz-mur. You should search the corpses of Orcs in the passage for signs of what caused them to die.\n2\tCompleted\tThe defilers and their masters used lesser Orcs as tasters for the poisons brewed in Baiúrz-mur. The defilers' poison has been carefully brewed to take down any living creature, even the hardy Orcs.\n",
[8324]="7005CBD9\n1\tSearch for the old market\tDashât-zahar is in western Clovengap. You should search for Dashât-zahar, an old market.\n2\tReturn to Gerja\tGerja Defthand is in south-west Clovengap. You should let Gerja Defthand know what you found in the old market.\n",
[8325]="70028B7E\n1\tCollect a map from the Draig-lûth\tThe Draig-lûth can be found in Thrór's Coomb in Enedwaith. Frithgeir asked you to search the Draig-lûth in Thrór's Coomb to see if you can find a map indicating where they are taking their treasure.\n2\tShow the map to Frithgeir\tFrithgeir is at Zudrugund in Thrór's Coomb in Enedwaith. The map is full of scribbles and nonsense. Perhaps Frithgeir will be able to help you decipher it.\n3\tShow Nár the map you found\tNár is in the library at Zudrugund in Thrór's Coomb in Enedwaith. Frithgeir examined the map and found nothing he could decipher. He suggested you bring it down to Nár in the library and see if he could make anything of it.\n4\tFrithgeir is at Zudrugund in Thrór's Coomb in Enedwaith. Nár mumbled what seemed to be a bunch of nonsense while scribbling on the map. Hopefully, Frithgeir can help to translate the mad dwarf's ramblings.\t\n",
[8326]="7005D361\n1\tSearch for Anatrâd\030Search for the fields of Frósthel\030Search for the look-out\030Search for the Amgaruslun Falls\tThe new locations are in northern Clovengap. You should search for the Amgaruslun Falls, the ruins of Anatrâd, the look-out, and Frósthel.\n2\tReturn to Gerja\tGerja Defthand is in Bazanmanar, in north-east Clovengap. You should let Gerja Defthand know what you found.\n",
[8327]="7002D7AA\n1\tHead to the first section of the Winding Way and draw on the parchment\tThe Winding Way is to the east, and connects the Chamber of the Cross-roads with the Twenty-first Hall. Thálfi has asked you to map the Winding Way and Twenty-first Hall to the east of the Chamber of the Cross-roads.\n2\tHead to the second section of the Winding Way and draw on the parchment\tThe Winding Way is to the east, and connects the Chamber of the Cross-roads with the Twenty-first Hall. Thálfi has asked you to map the Winding Way and Twenty-first Hall to the east of the Chamber of the Cross-roads.\n3\tHead to the third section of the Winding Way and draw on the parchment\tThe Winding Way is to the east, and connects the Chamber of the Cross-roads with the Twenty-first Hall. Thálfi has asked you to map the Winding Way and Twenty-first Hall to the east of the Chamber of the Cross-roads.\n4\tHead to the fourth section of the Winding Way and draw on the parchment\tThe Winding Way is to the east, and connects the Chamber of the Cross-roads with the Twenty-first Hall. Thálfi has asked you to map the Winding Way and Twenty-first Hall to the east of the Chamber of the Cross-roads.\n5\tHead to the final section of the Winding Way and draw on the parchment\tThe Winding Way is to the east, and connects the Chamber of the Cross-roads with the Twenty-first Hall. Thálfi has asked you to map the Winding Way and Twenty-first Hall to the east of the Chamber of the Cross-roads.\n6\tEnter the Twenty-first Hall and draw it on the parchment to complete the map\tThe Winding Way is to the east, and connects the Chamber of the Cross-roads with the Twenty-first Hall. Thálfi has asked you to map the Winding Way and Twenty-first Hall to the east of the Chamber of the Cross-roads.\n7\tSpeak to Thálfi in the Chamber of the Cross-roads\tThálfi is to the west at the the Chamber of the Cross-roads. Thálfi is waiting for you to return with the map you have drawn of the Winding Way.\n",
[8328]="7004DA4B\n1\tDefeat Jangovar marauders (total: 6)\tJangovar marauders can be found in the wilds near the city of Dale in the Dale-lands. Erna has asked you to defeat any Jangovar marauders you come across.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have defeated many Jangovar marauders.\n",
[8329]="70021D87\n1\tDefeat Wargs in Nan Laeglin (total: 8)\030Defeat half-orcs in Nan Laeglin (total: 8)\tWargs and half-orcs from Isengard can be found throughout Nan Laeglin, especially where they have raided Uch-lûth farmsteads. Siorus Brehur has asked you to defend his people against the marauding Wargs and half-orcs in the region of Nan Laeglin.\n2\tTalk to Siorus Brehur at the Brenin's Hall\tSiorus Brehur is at the Brenin's Hall in the village of Lhanuch. You should return to Siorus Brehur with news of your victory.\n",
[8330]="7000E83A\n1\tDefeat half-orcs in Nain Enidh (total: 15)\tHalf-orcs can be found throughout the Nain Enidh region of the Lone-lands, far to the east of Bree. Nidgyl has asked you to defeat the half-orcs marauding in the Lone-lands.\n2\tTalk to Nidgyl\tNidgyl is at Bree-town in Bree-land, far to the west of Nain Enidh. You should return to Nidgyl of Bree-town and tell him of your battles against the half-orcs of Nain Enidh.\n",
[8331]="700588B2\n1\tComplete 'March on Gundabad: Securing the Slade'\030Complete 'March on Gundabad: Healing Hands'\030Complete 'March on Gundabad: Resupplying the Forces'\030Complete 'March on Gundabad: Torching the Trenches'\030Complete 'March on Gundabad: Siege Upon Siege Engines'\030Complete 'March on Gundabad: Pilfering Orkish Orders'\030Complete 'March on Gundabad: Raising Morale'\tHlóthi has requested your aid in completing several tasks outside of Gundabad for the Gabil'akkâ, the Unified Army of Dwarves. NOTE: In order to advance this quest, you must complete any four of the required quests.\n2\tTalk to Hlóthi\tLocate Hlóthi and inform him of your progress.\n",
[8332]="70058751\n1\tComplete missions (total: 3)\tHlóthi has asked for your assistance in the war effort. The Gabil'akkâ, the Unified Army of Dwarves, has requested that you assist the war effort.\n2\tSpeak to Hlóthi\tYour assistance in completing several sorties for the Gabil'akkâ has been greatly noticed.\n",
[8333]="700588AC\n1\tTend to (total: 7) injured soldiers\tYou can find injured soldiers scattered across enemy territory, beyond the dwarves' trenches at Ifbar-athrâkh. More soldiers have been stranded in Azgh-buzru, but Hlóthi has suggested bringing allies if you go there. You should tend to these soldiers' wounds so that they may return to safety.\n2\tTalk to Hlóthi\tThe soldiers you tended to will seek treatment from the healers. Hlóthi in Annâk-khurfu will want to know that you've honoured his request.\n",
[8334]="70058783\n1\tComplete missions (total: 3)\tSeek out and complete several missions to assist the Gabil'akkâ.\n2\tSpeak to Elóf\tSeek out and speak to Elóf regarding your completion of several missions.\n",
[8335]="700588B0\n1\tCollect elite Orkish orders (total: 3)\030Collect Orkish orders (total: 8)\tOrkish orders can be found across the War of Three Peaks. You should gather Orkish orders to help the Gabil'akkâ's cause.\n2\tReturn to Hlóthi\tHlóthi is in Annak-khurfu in southern Elderslade. Return to Hlóthi.\n",
[8336]="700588B1\n1\tThe dwarf-trenches have been dug along the main road towards Gundabad. Hlóthi has asked that you sing to disheartened soldiers in the trenches, so that you may bolster their spirits.\t\n2\tTalk to Hlóthi\tYou have sung songs for several disheartened soldiers and bolstered their spirits. Hlóthi in Zarkul-sulûn is waiting for you to report back.\n",
[8337]="700588AD\n1\tReplenish supply crates (total: 5)\tThere are empty supply crates in Shakal-atrâd, Ifbar-athrâkh, the trenches, and on the docked boat. You should deliver the supplies and replenish the crates. Shakal-atrâd lies to the north-east of Zarkul-sulûn, and Ifbar-athrâkh is close to the forward-most dwarf trench. The dwarf-trenches can be found along the main road towards Gundabad, and the boat near the lake's south-eastern shore.\n2\tTalk to Hlóthi\tYou have distributed fresh supplies among the Gabil'akkâ. Hlóthi awaits news in Zarkul-sulûn.\n",
[8338]="700588AB\n1\tDefeat foes in the War of Three Peaks (total: 20)\tFoes can be found throughout the War of Three Peaks. Hlóthi has asked you to defeat foes in the War of Three Peaks.\n2\tSpeak to Hlóthi\tHlóthi is in Annak-khurfu in southern Elderslade. Return to Hlóthi.\n",
[8339]="70058F9A\n1\tComplete 'Shakalush, the Stair Battle'\tHlóthi has requested your aid in securing Bagûd-mekhem, the Gate of Wind, for the Gabil'akkâ, the Unified Army of Dwarves.\n2\tSpeak to Hlóthi\tLocate Hlóthi and inform him of your progress.\n",
[8340]="700588AF\n1\tDestroy Orc ballistae (total: 3)\030Destroy Orc catapults (total: 3)\030Destroy Orc trebuchets (total: 3)\tSiege engines can be found throughout the War of Three Peaks. Hlóthi has tasked you with destroying enemy siege engines.\n2\tReturn to Hlóthi\tHlóthi is in Zarkul-sulûn, in southern Elderslade. Return to Hlóthi.\n",
[8341]="700588AE\n1\tPick up a powder keg\tEnemy trenches can be found across the War of Three Peaks. You should carry a powder keg to the enemy trenches.\n2\tSpeak with Hlóthi\tHlóthi is in Zarkul-sulûn in southern Elderslade. Return to Hlóthi.\n",
[8342]="70042957\n1\tAsk one of the Boffins about Marigold\tOne of the Boffins outside Prisca's house may know where Marigold has gone. You returned many of Prisca Boffin's children to her home, but Marigold Boffin is still out there somewhere.\n2\tDefeat roots in the Old Forest (total: 3)\030Defeat bats in the Old Forest (total: 3)\030Defeat wolves in the Old Forest (total: 3)\tMarigold Boffin may be lost somewhere in the Old Forest, and Angelica Boffin told you of the bats, roots, and wolves that might threaten her sister in the wood.\n3\tSearch along the banks of the Withywindle, in the Old Forest, for Marigold Boffin\tThe Withywindle River runs through the middle of the Old Forest, and might be a good landmark to use in your search for Marigold Boffin.\n4\tTalk to Bingo along the banks of the Withywindle, in the Old Forest\tYou and Bingo have found Marigold Boffin in the Old Forest, along the banks of the Withywindle.\n5\tTalk to Marigold along the banks of the Withywindle, in the Old Forest\tMarigold is excited to speak with you about Bingo's adventure. You and Bingo have found Marigold Boffin in the Old Forest, along the banks of the Withywindle.\n6\tFind the house of the strange creature with yellow boots, in the Old Forest\tA strange creature of the forest with yellow boots invited Marigold to his home to the north-east, and you should accompany her and make sure it is safe.\n7\tTalk to Marigold outside the house of Tom Bombadil\tMarigold Boffin is outside Tom Bombadil's house in the Old Forest, north-east of the Withywindle River.\n8\tTalk to Bingo outside the house of Tom Bombadil\tBingo is outside Tom Bombadil's house in the Old Forest, north-east of the Withywindle River.\n",
[8343]="7006422C\n1\tBring the letter to Aelindil in Tornhad\tAelindil can be found at Tornhad, in the Angle of Mitheithel. You have received a letter from Aelindil, a Mariner of the Dúnedain, who wishes to speak with you.\n",
[8344]="700272FF\n1\tCollect lake-side plants (total: 6)\tLake-side plants with red flowers can be found growing alongside the shore of the lake in Tâl Methedras, but only where the dirt comes right down to the water. Taf has asked you to collect lake-side plants with red leaves that he can grind up for dye.\n2\tBring lake-side plants to Taf\tTaf is at the leather-working pavillion in Tûr Morva. You have collected the lake-side plants Taf asked you to gather and should bring them to him.\n3\tGrind up some dye using Taf's grinding stone\tThere is a grinding stone at the leather-working pavillion near Taf, in Tûr Morva. Taf has asked you to grind up the plants you gathered on his grinding stone, in order to make the colouring for the dye he needs.\n4\tBring the crushed dye to Taf\tTaf is at the leather-working pavillion in Tûr Morva. You have ground up some dye on his grinding stone and should show the product of your labour to Taf.\n5\tDraw the mark of the Falcon clan on the partially-completed armour\tPartially-completed leather armour is on the table near Taf in the leather-working pavillion of Tûr Morva. Taf has asked you to use the dye you prepared to put the mark of the Falcon on some of the partially-completed leather armour he has set out on a table.\n6\tReturn the excess dye to Taf\tTaf is at the leather-working pavillion in Tûr Morva. You have drawn the mark of the Falcon on some of the partially-completed armour and should return the excess dye to Taf.\n",
[8345]="700395D6\n1\tLure and defeat Curr\tEgbalth's horn can be found outside one of the burned homes at Bosa's Farm. The leader of the White Hand forces at Bosa's Farm has not made himself known. You should sound Egbalth's horn to lure the Uruk leader to your position.\n2\tTalk to Thane Mágla\tThane Mágla can be found inside the Mead Hall of Middlemead. You have dispatched the Uruk leader, Curr, who spoke of something deeply unsettling before being defeated. You should return to Thane Mágla with this information.\n",
[8346]="7004CE47\n1\tCollect marked crates (total: 8)\tMarked crates can be found inside Esgaroth-of-old. You should collect marked crates.\n2\tTalk to Mervárth\tMervárth can be found outside Esgaroth-of-old. You should talk to Mervárth.\n",
[8347]="7006C08B\n1\tMark weaknesses in Jirush's walls (total: 5)\tThe walls in TBD Location need to be marked for repair, to the TBD direction. TBD Carpenter has asked for your help again, this time in marking the damaged parts of the battlements so he can repair them later.\n2\tReturn to TBD Carpenter\tTBD Carpenter can be found in TBD. You have left marks on the most decrepit parts of Jirush's battlements for the TBD Carpenter to repair later. Return to him with updates so he can begin his work soon.\n",
[8348]="70071CD2\n1\tSpeak with Merbâna in the Court of Larinâsta\tSpeak with Merbâna in the Court of Larinâsta in Zajâna about buying the book Khâbakh requested. The Court of Larinâsta is located due east of the Kalmakhíla, whilst still in Zajâna.\n2\tHaggle with Merbâna in the Court of Larinâsta\tHaggle with Merbâna in the Court of Larinâsta in Zajâna about how many oranges she needs in exchange for the book Khâbakh requested.\n3\tContinue haggling with Merbâna in the Court of Larinâsta\tContinue haggling with Merbâna in the Court of Larinâsta in Zajâna about how many oranges she needs in exchange for Khâbakh's book.\n4\tFinish haggling with Merbâna in the Court of Larinâsta\tFinish haggling with Merbâna in the Court of Larinâsta in Zajâna about how many oranges she needs in exchange for Khâbakh's book.\n5\tHarvest oranges outside Zajâna (total: 7)\tGo to the hillside outside the Khab Kitâx outside Zajâna where the orange trees grow and gather seven oranges for Merbâna.\n6\tReturn to Merbâna in Larinâsta in Zajâna with the oranges\tReturn to Merbâna in the Court of Larinâsta in Zajâna with the harvested oranges.\n7\tReturn to Khâbakh in the Kalmakhíla with the book\tReturn to Khâbakh in the Kalmakhíla in Zajâna with the book he requested. The Kalmakhíla can be found near the Shorakhúna in central Zajâna.\n",
[8349]="7004E843\n1\tFind a dwarf matching Dori's description in the New-lodes of Narathâk\tThe New-lodes of Narathâk can be found in the entry hall of Erebor. Believing him to be in league with Nori, Dori has asked you to find a dwarf of uncommon lineage in the New-lodes of Narathâk.\n2\tTalk to the dwarf in the New-lodes of Narathâk\tThe strange dwarf can be found among the New-lodes of Narathâk. You have found a dwarf matching Dori's description and should now speak to him.\n3\tDefeat deep-claws in the New-lodes of Narathâk (total: 6)\tDeep-claws have burrowed into the New-lodes of Narathâk. In exchange for aiding him in repelling the deep-claws of Erebor, Débel has offered to share what he knows of Nori's secret expedition to Thikil-gundu.\n4\tTalk to Débel in the New-lodes of Narathâk\tDébel can be found among the New-lodes of Narathâk. You have defeated many of the encroaching deep-claws in the New-lodes of Narathâk and should now return to Débel.\n5\tTalk to Dori in the Hall Under the Mountain\tDori can be found among the upper levels of the Hall under the Mountain. You have obtained a spare key to Nori's home in Erebor, and you should now return to Dori and tell him what you have learned.\n6\tMeet Dori at Nori's home in Tumnu-dûm, the Dwelling-halls\tNori's home can be found in Tumnu-dûm, the Dwelling-halls of Erebor. After learning that Nori left behind a spare key, Dori has asked you to meet him at Nori's home in Erebor.\n7\tUnlock the door to Nori's home and begin your search with Dori\tNori's home can be found in Tumnu-dûm, the Dwelling-halls of Erebor. You have arrived at Nori's home in Tumnu-dûm and should now use the spare key to gain entry.\n8\tTalk to Dori in Nori's home\tDori can be found inside Nori's home in Tumnu-dûm, the Dwelling-halls of Erebor. You have gained entry to Nori's home and should now speak to Dori.\n9\tNotes can be found throughout Nori's home in Tumnu-dûm, the Dwelling-halls of Erebor. After noticing a number of scattered notes, Dori has asked you to begin your search of his brother's home by examining what Nori left behind.\t\n10\tTalk to Dori in Nori's home\tDori can be found inside Nori's home in Tumnu-dûm, the Dwelling-halls of Erebor. You have examined many notes in Nori's home and they bear marks of a conspiracy to defy the King under the Mountain and seek the hoards of Thikil-gundu. You should inform Dori.\n11\tTalk to Dori before the throne of King Thorin III\tDori can be found before the throne of King Thorin III in the Hall under the Mountain. Dori intends to beg King Thorin III to allow him to seek his brother, Nori, in the Ered Mithrin. You should meet Dori before the throne of King Thorin III.\n12\tTalk to King Thorin III\tKing Thorin III can be found before his throne in the Hall under the Mountain. Dori has begged King Thorin III to grant him leave to pursue his brother into the Ered Mithrin. You should now speak to King Thorin III.\n13\tTalk to Dori\tDori can be found before the throne of King Thorin III in the Hall under the Mountain. King Thorin III has granted Dori leave to pursue Nori into the Ered Mithrin, but Dori must now meet his terms. You should speak to Dori.\n",
[8350]="70041863\n1\tWeaken masts of Corsair ships\tCorsair ships can be found at the docks of Ethillorn in western Lower Lebennin. You have found many Corsair ships at Ethillorn and should weaken their masts before they set sail once more.\n2\tWeaken masts of docked Corsair ships (total: 12)\tCorsair ships can be found at the docks of Ethillorn in western Lower Lebennin. You have found many Corsair ships at Ethillorn and should weaken their masts before they set sail once more.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have weakened the masts of many Corsair ships at Ethillorn.\n",
[8351]="70041376\n1\tDefeat spirits in the Dead Marshes (total: 15)\tSome disturbance has wakened many of the dead within the marshes. These spirits will work no good in the world while they prowl. You should defeat a number of fell spirits in the Dead Marshes.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have defeated a number of spirits in the Dead Marshes.\n",
[8352]="7002FD07\n1\tCollect marsh reeds (total: 8)\tMarsh reeds tend to grow along the edges of standing water, and prefer the rich soil near bogs. You should collect marsh reeds, the favourite food of Harwick's horses.\n2\tBring the marsh reeds to Céolstan at the Harwick Stables\tThe guard of the stables waits for you to return.\n",
})
